Very true. And the UN RNG provided me three(!) (or was it even four?) of
those stethoscopes before I diluted a potion and got that djinn wish. ;-)

I mean, really, if all objects that makes sense to get from those wishes
are just two or three items, I'd rather remove those wishes completely.
This dialog with the djinn was a really annoying experience.

>> So I could NOT get dragon armor, rings of conflict, boots of speed, no
>> spellbook of magic missile, no gauntlets of power, amulet of reflection,
>> no marker, it seems generally no amulets, no rings, I didn't try wands.
>> The point is; once you're equipped enough to take the risk of dipping,
>> you rarely need any non-magical item any more.
> 
> Even in Vanilla fountain dipping is not a good mean for completing
> your ascension kit.

Sure, but if you get a wish in Vanilla you get your choice from all (but
two or three) items, not vice versa. (I mean, effectively there's no more
than a few non-magical items worth wishing, especially since you dip only
if you are buff enough to handle the outcome (otherwise you'll probably
die anyway, as I mentioned) you probably already have those three items.
In UN this is even more likely than in Vanilla, as I noticed, since there
is that town level (in addition to the minetown with its shops) with a lot
of additional helpful non-magical items, and especially the tools shops are
the major source of non-magical helpful items.

